\par\par \b \uc2  Banco de Mexico says peso to float for time being. \b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, March 9 (Reuter) - The Mexican peso will remain floating for the time being, and no plans have been made yet to change the exchange rate regime, a Banco de Mexico spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  "For the time being, the exchange scheme for \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  is free floatation with discretionary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the spokesman, who asked not to be identified, said. He denied there were any plans to impose exchange controls, as has been rumoured in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets where the peso plummeted. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only start thinking about possible alternative peso regimes when conditions improve. \par \par \uc2  The spokesman declined to put a timeframe on when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected conditions to be suitable for a new exchange rate policy, but he suggested the decision was not imminent. \par \par \uc2  Officials, including the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman, are expecting the government to announce new emergency measures to deal with the peso crisis by the latest Friday. \par \par \uc2  -- Henry Tricks, Mexico City bureau +525 728-9560 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr3900fyo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
