\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's New Peso Closes Sharply Down At 6.7950 To Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 20:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's new peso continued its downward plunge against the dollar Tuesday, finishing at its weakest closing level ever against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot and 24-hour dollar markets, the dollar ended at mid rate levels of 6.7950 new pesos per dollar against 6.5750 new pesos per dollar at Monday's close. Spreads were 6.7700/6.8200 new pesos per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Monday's close had been a previous all-time closing low for the new peso against the dollar. The dollar also soared to an intraday historic high of 7.0250 new pesos/dlr Monday amid continuing political and economic uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  Traders said it was probable \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday around 1730 GMT, when the dollar hit 6.8500 new pesos/dlr. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not be confirmed. \par \par \uc2  Market traders estimated the Bank of Mexico bought $350 million worth of new pesos Monday to bring the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below seven pesos to the dollar. That also could not be confirmed. \par \par \uc2  Market volume Tuesday was average, with the peso suffering as investors continued to fret over a seeming lack of economic and political direction, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  'Nobody is bringing dollars to Mexico,' said one Mexico City trader. 'With this kind of volatility, there is no way you can hedge your bets.' \par \par \uc2  The peso also was bruised in cross-trading as the dollar continued to lose significant ground against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said traders. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-03-95 \par \par \uc2  1948GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3701n6d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
