\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico new peso ends sharply down, off worst levels. \b0\par\par\uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, March 6 (Reuter) - Mexico's new peso closed sharply weaker on continued fears over the Mexican economy, but off its lows after the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to prop up the faltering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The new peso closed 25 centavos weaker at 6.53/6.58 per dollar in 24-hour and 48-hour contracts, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "It was pure speculation ... everyone began to buy dollars because of the economic and political uncertainty here," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  "Later in the day, the Banco de Mexico entered the market and it stopped the peso's fall," he said. \par \par \uc2  One trader said investors bailed out of the peso on rumors that a government takeover on Friday of Banpais bank could be repeated with a handful of other banks facing debt problems. \par \par \uc2  But some analysts said the peso suffered because of a world-wide speculative attack on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that are considered weak following the devaluation Sunday of the Spanish peseta. \par \par \uc2  "The peseta devaluation mixed with ongoing concerns over the Mexican economy, including the health of banks," one Mexico City analyst told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they estimated Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent about $200 million defending the peso. Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there was still heavy dollar demand at the end of the trading day, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The same-day new peso closed 88 centavos weaker at 6.80/6.90 per dollar earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokum