\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's New Peso Ends At New Low Vs. Dlr At 6.5750 \b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 20:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's new peso fell to its lowest closing level ever versus the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, dropping 27 centavos against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot and 24-hour dollar markets, the dollar ended at middle rate levels of 6.5750 new pesos per dollar against 6.3050 new pesos per dollar at Friday's close. Spreads were 6.5500/6.6000 new pesos per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit an intraday high of 7.0250 pesos/dlr around 1630 GMT - the dollar's highest rate ever against the new peso - before the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded somewhat in the final three hours of trading. Dealers said it was likely \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the sagging peso. That couldn't be confirmed, however. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit a previous intraday high of 6.5500 pesos/dlr on Jan. 30, one day before U.S. President Bill Clinton announced a $50-billion multilateral credit package for Mexico. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finished at an all-time closing high of 6.3050 new pesos/dlr last Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said volume was moderate Monday, with speculative trading prompting volatile swings throughout the day in the absence of any new government announcements regarding revised economic targets. Perceived political instability also hurt the peso, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  Traders in New York said the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also was being hit hard by the continuing fall of the dollar against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , prompting investors to convert the peso into German Deutsche mark and Japanese yen by cross-trading with the dollar. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-03-95 \par \par \uc2  1945GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3601m1t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
