\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's New Peso Closes Weaker At 5.9750 To Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 1995\par 21:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's new peso closed 3 centavos lower against the dollar in light trading Tuesday as the peso continued to flirt with the six new pesos to the dollar level. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot and 24-hour dollar markets, the dollar ended at middle rate levels of 5.9750 new pesos per dollar against 5.9450 new pesos per dollar at Monday's close. Spreads were 5.9500/6.0000 new pesos per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders said most \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players were awaiting a government announcement on a revised economic program before making any major moves. \par \par \uc2  The prospect that government officials won't be able to hammer out a new wage-price control agreement with business and labor leaders nonetheless exerted a slight downward pressure on the peso, they added. The current 'Pacto,' forged Jan. 3 under emergency conditions, is due to expire at the end of the week. \par \par \uc2  Traders said it also was likely \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ensure the new peso didn't break through the psychological barrier of 6 new pesos to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has in the past been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at that level. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-02-95 \par \par \uc2  2012GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr2s01fh0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
