\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's New Peso Closes Stronger At 5.7250 To Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 1995\par 20:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's new peso reversed four days of steep declines against the dollar Friday to close 35 centavos stronger in light activity. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot and 24-hour dollar markets, the dollar ended at middle rate levels of 5.7250 new pesos per dollar against 6.0750 new pesos per dollar at Thursday's close. Spreads were 5.7000/5.7500 new pesos per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there was strong speculation \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the quiet market Friday to help return the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below the psychological barrier of 6 new pesos to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  couldn't immediately be confirmed. \par \par \uc2  A one-time \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offer to pay off some $2 billion in dollar-linked Tesobonos next week may have provided further incentive for an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they added. A stronger peso makes it cheaper for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay off those obligations. \par \par \uc2  The new peso was also helped by speculation that Mexican Finance Minister Guillermo Ortiz could announce in coming days a final accord on a $20-billion U.S. credit package he was negotiating in Washington, as well as an apparent turn to quiet in the insurrection-wracked southern state of Chiapas, traders said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-02-95 \par \par \uc2  1948GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr2h013y6\par }\page {\p