\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Fed  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2 /Peso -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  Seeking Aid Elsewhere \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 1995\par 08:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The peso \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been partly designed to offset selling by investors who intend to bail out of this week's 683-million-dlr maturity in tesobonos, which are dollar-indexed bonds. The Federal Reserve action was complemented by a sharp rise in overnight-interest rates by Banco de Mexico to 50%. \par \par \uc2  The rate boost in Mexico was aimed at keeping Mexican investors from selling pesos as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved sharply higher against the dollar for the first time in days. \par \par \uc2  The sudden appearance of bilateral cooperation in the markets, along with the draw-down of credit lines by Mexico, may point to new cash needs. Not only does the government need dollars to roll over the huge tesobono positions, but apparently Mexican banks and corporations may also have difficulty paying off dollar debts. \par \par \uc2  Analysts here say that Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be extending dollar credit lines to some banks to help them pay off dollar certificates of deposits and other obligations. Later, analysts expect many corporations to seek similar government \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  aid. But reports say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves are now below 6 billion dlrs. \par \par \uc2  Since the 18 billion dlrs in international credit lines just about covers foreign holdings in tesobonos, Mexico will have to find a new source of financial aid. Analysts figure for this reason Mexico's foreign minister Jose Angel Gurria is in Japan trying to line up additional short-term emergency financing. \par \par \uc2  Also, a team from the International Monetary Fund prepared to begin talks in Mexico City this week toward negotiating a standby-credit arrangement. \par \par \uc2  Whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , along with the recently unveiled Mexican reforms and the soon-to-be negotiated IMF agreement, ends the investor panic, remains to be seen. For example, Scudder's Cornell, though relieved, doesn't envision an immediate buying spree in Mexican markets. 'This wasn't trivial,' she said. 'I'm going to wait and watch a little.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-01-95 \par \par \uc2  0701GMT \par \par \uc2  1127 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr1a002pm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
