\par\par \b \uc2  N.Y. Fed/Mexico/Amplifier -2: Draws On Rescue Package \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 1995\par 00:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Also Monday, the Bank of Mexico announced it had made its first drawing on the 18 billion dollar rescue package put up by the U.S., Canada and other industrialized countries, as well as certain commercial banks. The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it drew 500 million dollars from the U.S. standby facility and 83 million CDN dlrs from the Canadian facility. \par \par \uc2  It wasn't clear whether the amounts drawn were used by the Fed in Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though traders said the Fed's peso buying was relatively light. The drawings may also have been used to bolster Mexico's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which had fallen to 5.55 billion dlrs by the end of last week. \par \par \uc2  In an unusual move, the Fed announced that it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peso early in the New York trading day, before the official opening of Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Fed purchases of new pesos in the open market were unprecedented, according to some analysts. \par \par \uc2  The announcement pushed the dollar as low as 4.9050 new pesos when Mexican markets opened, but the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  quickly reversed course as it ran into further selling pressure. That drew other rounds of Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around midday in New York, also on behalf of the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the Fed sighted selling dollars to U.S. banks at around 5.0000 new pesos and 5.1000 new pesos. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the public announcement was probably an attempt to get the maximum possible leverage out of the Fed's entry into the market, the first reported \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  effort to prop up the peso since Mexico's decision to float the new peso on Dec. 21. \par \par \uc2  After the Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed secondary money market rates to climb to 50%, buying overnight Cetes repurchase agreements at that rate. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-01-95 \par \par \uc2  2322GMT \par \par \uc2  1146 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr19002d9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
