\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico/Repos At 50% -2: To Shore Up New Peso \b0\par\par\uc2 125 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 1995\par 18:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--The Bank of Mexico successfully bought 963 million new pesos of 1-day repurchase agreements for Cetes, Bondes and inflation-indexed Ajustabonos at a rate of 50%, secondary money market traders said Monday. \par \par \uc2  The rate represents a sharp increase in secondary money market rates and reflects a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempt to shore up the new peso, they said. Though firm on the day in reaction to New York Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's account, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues under pressure, quoted at 5.25 pesos per dollar, weaker than the Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of 5.000 new pesos per dollar. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-01-95 \par \par \uc2  1738GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr190025w\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (mexico near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \cl